{
 "about": "Lot 310 (external bug hunt, edition 1.4: BUG-97, BUG-99, BUG-100, BUG-104's sibling, N3; the mini-hunt's variants): a user's process reads ~/.aws/credentials under the name `aws` while it runs a script of /tmp or an inline program, and names /usr/bin/aws only as an argument its interpreter's options consume \u2014 bash's long options with one hyphen (-noprofile, -rcfile F, -norc -login), node's --eval=, --print=, --run, zsh's and mksh's -o with its name attached, busybox as sh \u2014 each NN-L-FIM-011 (High, KillProcess). Control: the real client (python3 running /usr/bin/aws) reads its store, nothing. On main each misread argv was taken for the aws client and the rule was silent.",
